      "Language": "eng",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "We describe a 35-year-old woman with arthralgias and skin lesions suggesting sarcoidosis. No pulmonary lesions were present. The diagnosis was established by histological examination of a swollen and discolored scar. We review the literature of \"scar sarcoidosis\" and discuss the similarities between this entity and silica granuloma."},
